      "kind": "editorial",
      "status": "blocked",
      "issues": [
        "- In the Greek/Latin Roots table, the row for \"pro-\" incorrectly lists \"re-\" as an opposite prefix; \"re-\" means \"again/back\", not \"against\". The true antonym of pro- is \"anti-\" (or \"contra-\"). → Remove \"re-\" from the antonym column; only \"anti-\" is the opposite.",
        "- In the same table, the row for \"phil-\" gives \"mis-\" as the root for \"hate\" in \"misanthropy\"; the Greek root for hate is \"miso-\", while \"mis-\" is a Latin/English prefix meaning \"bad/wrong\". → Change \"mis- (घृणा)\" to \"miso- (घृणा)\" and note that \"misanthropy\" derives from Greek \"misos\" (hatred)."
      ],
